   1:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_can.c **** /**
   2:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_can.c ****   ******************************************************************************
   3:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_can.c ****   * @file    stm32f4xx_can.c
   4:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_can.c ****   * @author  MCD Application Team
   5:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_can.c ****   * @version V1.8.0
   6:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_can.c ****   * @date    04-November-2016
   7:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_can.c ****   * @brief   This file provides firmware functions to manage the following 
   8:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_can.c ****   *          functionalities of the Controller area network (CAN) peripheral:
   9:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_can.c ****   *           + Initialization and Configuration 
  10:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_can.c ****   *           + CAN Frames Transmission
  11:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_can.c ****   *           + CAN Frames Reception
  12:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_can.c ****   *           + Operation modes switch
  13:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_can.c ****   *           + Error management
  14:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_can.c ****   *           + Interrupts and flags
  15:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_can.c ****   *
  16:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_can.c **** @verbatim
  17:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_can.c ****  ===============================================================================
  18:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_can.c ****                         ##### How to use this driver #####
  19:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_can.c ****  ===============================================================================
  20:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_can.c ****     [..]
  21:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_can.c ****       (#) Enable the CAN controller interface clock using 
  22:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_can.c ****           RCC_APB1PeriphClockCmd(RCC_APB1Periph_CAN1, ENABLE); for CAN1 
  23:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_can.c ****           and RCC_APB1PeriphClockCmd(RCC_APB1Periph_CAN2, ENABLE); for CAN2
  24:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_can.c ****       -@- In case you are using CAN2 only, you have to enable the CAN1 clock.
  25:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_can.c ****        
  26:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_can.c ****       (#) CAN pins configuration
  27:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_can.c ****         (++) Enable the clock for the CAN GPIOs using the following function:
  28:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_can.c ****              RCC_AHB1PeriphClockCmd(RCC_AHB1Periph_GPIOx, ENABLE);   
  29:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_can.c ****         (++) Connect the involved CAN pins to AF9 using the following function 
  30:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_can.c ****              GPIO_PinAFConfig(GPIOx, GPIO_PinSourcex, GPIO_AF_CANx); 
ARM GAS  /tmp/cclurMk5.s 			page 2


  31:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_can.c ****         (++) Configure these CAN pins in alternate function mode by calling
  32:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_can.c ****              the function  GPIO_Init();
  33:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_can.c ****       
  34:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_can.c ****       (#) Initialize and configure the CAN using CAN_Init() and 
  35:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_can.c ****           CAN_FilterInit() functions.   
  36:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_can.c ****                  
  37:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_can.c ****       (#) Transmit the desired CAN frame using CAN_Transmit() function.
  38:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_can.c ****            
  39:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_can.c ****       (#) Check the transmission of a CAN frame using CAN_TransmitStatus()
  40:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_can.c ****           function.
  41:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_can.c ****                  
  42:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_can.c ****       (#) Cancel the transmission of a CAN frame using CAN_CancelTransmit()
  43:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_can.c ****           function.  
  44:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_can.c ****               
  45:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_can.c ****       (#) Receive a CAN frame using CAN_Receive() function.
  46:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_can.c ****            
  47:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_can.c ****       (#) Release the receive FIFOs using CAN_FIFORelease() function.
  48:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_can.c ****                  
  49:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_can.c ****       (#) Return the number of pending received frames using 
  50:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_can.c ****           CAN_MessagePending() function.            
  51:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_can.c ****                      
  52:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_can.c ****       (#) To control CAN events you can use one of the following two methods:
  53:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_can.c ****         (++) Check on CAN flags using the CAN_GetFlagStatus() function.  
  54:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_can.c ****         (++) Use CAN interrupts through the function CAN_ITConfig() at 
  55:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_can.c ****              initialization phase and CAN_GetITStatus() function into 
  56:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_can.c ****              interrupt routines to check if the event has occurred or not.
  57:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_can.c ****              After checking on a flag you should clear it using CAN_ClearFlag()
  58:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_can.c ****              function. And after checking on an interrupt event you should 
  59:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_can.c ****              clear it using CAN_ClearITPendingBit() function.            
  60:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_can.c **** 
  61:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_can.c **** @endverbatim
